            },
            "text": "Account Takeover (ATO) fraud involves unauthorized access to user accounts, typically through compromised credentials or session hijacking. ATLAS, a spatio-temporal graph framework, addresses ATO detection by constructing a **time-respecting directed session graph** with edges representing user interactions (e.g., login attempts) and nodes representing sessions. Connectivity is regulated by a **time window (T)** (e.g., 1–120 days) and **recency cap (K)** (e.g., 1–10 recent sessions).",
