            "embedding_text": "Authority: Account_Takeover\n\n        Document: 2509.20339v1\n\n        Chapter:\n        \n        \n\n        Section:\n        \n\n        Heading:\n        \n\n        Content:\n\n        Account Takeover (ATO) fraud involves unauthorized access to user accounts, typically through compromised credentials or session hijacking. ATLAS, a spatio-temporal graph framework, addresses ATO detection by constructing a **time-respecting directed session graph** with edges representing user interactions (e.g., login attempts) and nodes representing sessions. Connectivity is regulated by a **time window (T)** (e.g., 1–120 days) and **recency cap (K)** (e.g., 1–10 recent sessions)."
